            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous atherectomy catheters.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>373-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous atherectomy catheters have been developed as an alternative to balloon angioplasty for the treatment of atherosclerotic disease. This article summarizes the preliminary experimental and clinical results with these catheters.</AbstractText>
